(function(E){ const x = E["hr-m3"] = E["hr-m3"] || {units:{}}; x.units["hr-3-4"] = {"explain":{"id":"c-hr-3-4-e","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-4","type":"explain","level":"B1","title":{"en":"Offers and rejections","tr":"Teklifler ve olumsuz yanıtlar","fa":"پیشنهاد کار و ایمیل عدم پذیرش"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can make a job offer by phone and write a kind, clear rejection.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda telefonla iş teklifi yapabilecek, nazik ve net bir ret e-postası yazabileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی پیشنهاد کار را تلفنی بدهی و یک ایمیل عدم پذیرش محترمانه و روشن بنویسی."},"hook":{"en":"Give the news clearly, then add something kind. How you do it affects what people say about your company. Leyla's first draft was true, but it felt cold to Karim. Two tools made it kind.","tr":"Haberi net ver, sonra nazik bir şey ekle. Bunu nasıl yaptığın, insanların şirketin hakkında ne söyleyeceğini etkiler. Leyla’nın ilk taslağı doğruydu ama Karim’e soğuk geldi. İki araç onu nazik yaptı.","fa":"خبر را روشن بده و بعد چیزی مهربانانه اضافه کن. اینکه چطور این کار را می‌کنی، روی حرف مردم درباره‌ی شرکتت اثر می‌گذارد. پیش‌نویس اول لیلا درست بود، ولی برای کریم سرد بود. دو ابزار آن را مهربان کرد."},"before":{"en":"Write the first two lines of a rejection email: the clear news, then one true and specific thing the person did well.","tr":"Bir ret e-postasının ilk iki satırını yaz: net haber, ardından kişinin iyi yaptığı doğru ve somut bir şey.","fa":"دو خط اول یک ایمیل رد درخواست را بنویس: خبر روشن و بعد یک چیز واقعی و مشخص که آن شخص خوب انجام داد."},"rounds":[[1,4],[2,3]],"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Key points","tr":"Ana nokta","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifade","fa":"عبارت کلیدی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Practice tasks","tr":"Alıştırma","fa":"تمرین"},"value":"4"}],"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"The skill","tr":"Beceri","fa":"مهارت"},"head":{"en":"Say the news clearly, then be kind","tr":"Haberi net söyle, sonra nazik ol","fa":"خبر را روشن بگو و بعد مهربان باش"},"body":{"en":"A long, vague message makes a person guess. So give the news early, in one clear sentence. Then add something true and specific. Kindness comes from details, not from hiding the no.","tr":"Uzun ve belirsiz bir mesaj insanı tahmine zorlar. Bu yüzden haberi erken ve tek net cümleyle ver. Sonra doğru ve somut bir şey ekle. Nezaket, olumsuz cevabı saklamaktan değil, ayrıntılardan gelir.","fa":"پیام طولانی و مبهم آدم را به حدس زدن می‌اندازد. پس خبر را زود و در یک جمله‌ی روشن بگو. بعد چیزی واقعی و مشخص اضافه کن. مهربانی از جزئیات می‌آید، نه از پنهان کردن جواب منفی."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The language","tr":"Dil","fa":"زبان"},"head":{"en":"Softening bad news: I'm afraid + the passive","tr":"Kötü haberi yumuşatmak: I'm afraid + edilgen yapı","fa":"نرم کردن خبر بد: I’m afraid و مجهول"},"steps":[{"en":"Prepare the reader: I'm afraid, unfortunately, on this occasion.","tr":"Okuru hazırla: I'm afraid, unfortunately, on this occasion.","fa":"خواننده را آماده کن: I'm afraid، unfortunately، ⁨on this occasion⁩.","ex":"I'm afraid that on this occasion..."},{"en":"Passive: has been / was + past participle.","tr":"Edilgen: has been / was + past participle.","fa":"مجهول با has been یا was و اسم مفعول ساخته می‌شود.","ex":"The position has been offered to another candidate."},{"en":"Keep one clear sentence that says no.","tr":"'Hayır' diyen net bir cümle mutlaka olsun.","fa":"حتماً یک جمله‌ی روشن بگذار که «نه» را بگوید.","ex":"...the position has been offered to another candidate."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Move","Example"],"tr":["Hamle","Örnek"],"fa":["حرکت","مثال"]},"rows":[["Thank","Thank you for your time and interest."],["Soften","I'm afraid that on this occasion..."],["Say no (passive)","...the position has been offered to another candidate."],["Something specific and kind","We enjoyed hearing about how you trained new drivers."]]},"tip":{"en":"Turkish uses -ildi ('pozisyon başka bir adaya verildi') and Persian shode ast, so the passive idea is familiar. The trap is dropping been: English needs has been + past participle.","tr":"Türkçede edilgen '-ildi' ile yapılır: 'Pozisyon başka bir adaya verildi.' Anlam tanıdıktır; tuzak been'i unutmaktır: has been offered.","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «این موقعیت به متقاضی دیگری داده شد» و ساختار مجهول آشناست. تله این است که been را جا بیندازی: «has been offered»."},"wrong":"The role has offered to another candidate.","right":"The role has been offered to another candidate."},{"eyebrow":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های کلیدی"},"head":{"en":"Phrases for this task","tr":"Bu görev için ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های این کار"},"phrases":[{"phrase":"I'm calling with good news.","meaning":{"en":"Opens an offer call.","tr":"Teklif görüşmesini açar.","fa":"تماسِ پیشنهاد کار را شروع می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"The offer is subject to...","meaning":{"en":"States a condition.","tr":"Bir koşul belirtir.","fa":"یک شرط را می‌گوید."}},{"phrase":"I'm afraid that on this occasion...","meaning":{"en":"Softens a no without hiding it.","tr":"Hayırı saklamadan yumuşatır.","fa":"«نه» را نرم می‌کند، بدون اینکه پنهانش کند."}},{"phrase":"feedback","meaning":{"en":"Comments on how well someone did.","tr":"geri bildirim.","fa":"بازخورد"}}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"At work","tr":"İş yerinde","fa":"در محیط کار"},"head":{"en":"Silence hurts your reputation","tr":"Cevapsız bırakmak itibarını zedeler","fa":"بی‌جواب گذاشتن به اعتبار شرکت ضربه می‌زند"},"body":{"en":"In many UK and US companies, candidates rejected at the final stage often get a short call or an offer of feedback, while earlier-stage candidates get an email. In many markets candidates simply hear nothing, which hurts the employer's reputation. A short, kind, specific message takes five minutes.","tr":"Birçok İngiliz ve Amerikan şirketinde son aşamada elenen adaylar çoğu zaman kısa bir telefon ya da geri bildirim teklifi alır; daha erken aşamadakiler e-posta alır. Birçok pazarda adaylara hiç dönüş yapılmaz ve bu işverenin itibarına zarar verir. Kısa, nazik ve somut bir mesaj beş dakika sürer.","fa":"در بسیاری از شرکت‌های بریتانیا و آمریکا، متقاضیانی که در مرحله‌ی آخر انتخاب نمی‌شوند معمولاً یک تماس کوتاه یا پیشنهاد بازخورد می‌گیرند و متقاضیان مراحل اول یک ایمیل. در خیلی از بازارهای کار هم اصلاً هیچ جوابی به متقاضی داده نمی‌شود؛ تجربه‌ای که شاید برای تو هم آشنا باشد و به اعتبار کارفرما ضربه می‌زند. یک پیام کوتاه، مهربان و مشخص فقط پنج دقیقه وقت می‌گیرد."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"From weak to strong","tr":"Zayıftan güçlüye","fa":"از پیام سرد تا «نه»ی روشن و مهربان"},"text":"Facts: The role went to another candidate. This person spoke well about their safety work.","item":"Your application was unsuccessful. Do not reply to this email.","why":{"en":"Weak: cold, with nothing personal. Strong: one clear no, and one true detail.","tr":"Zayıf: soğuk, kişiye özel hiçbir şey yok. Güçlü: net bir hayır ve doğru bir ayrıntı.","fa":"نسخه‌ی اول سرد است و هیچ چیز شخصی ندارد. نسخه‌ی دوم «نه» را روشن می‌گوید و یک نکته‌ی واقعی هم اضافه می‌کند."},"answer":"I'm afraid the role has gone to another candidate. We enjoyed hearing about your safety work.","cut":["Do not reply to this email."],"cutHint":{"en":"Tap the line that shuts the door on the person.","tr":"Kişinin yüzüne kapıyı kapatan satıra dokun.","fa":"روی خطی بزن که در را به روی آن آدم می‌بندد."}},"quick":{"prompt":"A final-stage candidate was not chosen. What do many UK and US employers do?","options":["Give a short call or offer feedback","Send nothing: silence is kinder","Wait until the next job opens"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"A short call or an offer of feedback: silence hurts the employer’s reputation, and a short, kind, specific message takes five minutes.","tr":"Kısa bir telefon ya da geri bildirim teklifi: Sessizlik işverenin itibarına zarar verir; kısa, kibar ve somut bir mesaj beş dakika sürer.","fa":"یک تماس کوتاه یا پیشنهاد بازخورد: سکوت به اعتبار کارفرما ضربه می‌زند و یک پیام کوتاه، مهربان و مشخص فقط پنج دقیقه وقت می‌گیرد."},"point":4,"hint2":{"en":"Think about what a candidate remembers about a company after the last interview. What would make that memory fair?","tr":"Son görüşmeden sonra bir adayın şirket hakkında neyi hatırladığını düşün. Bu anıyı adil yapan ne olurdu?","fa":"فکر کن داوطلب بعد از آخرین مصاحبه چه چیزی از شرکت به یاد می‌آورد. چه چیزی این خاطره را منصفانه می‌کند؟"}},"remember":{"en":"Ask: who did the action? If the subject did not do it (the position, a decision), you need been. Result of this lesson: you can make an offer by phone and say no kindly. You also have a rejection email.","tr":"Sor: eylemi kim yaptı? Özne yapmadıysa (the position, a decision) been gerekir. Bu dersin sonucu: telefonla teklif yapabilir, olumsuz cevabı nazikçe verebilirsin ve elinde bir olumsuz yanıt e-postası olur.","fa":"بپرس: چه کسی کار را انجام داد؟ اگر فاعل جمله انجامش نداده (the position، a decision)، been لازم است. حالا می‌توانی تلفنی پیشنهاد کار بدهی و مهربانانه جواب منفی بدهی. ایمیل عدم پذیرش هم آماده است."},"b2Point":{"eyebrow":{"en":"B2 track","tr":"B2 yolu","fa":"مسیر B2"},"head":{"en":"Having considered...: perfect participle clauses","tr":"Having considered...: perfect participle yapıları","fa":"Having considered...: عبارت وصفی کامل"},"steps":[{"en":"Having + past participle = this was done first.","tr":"Having + past participle = bu önce yapıldı.","fa":"ساختار Having و اسم مفعول یعنی این کار اول انجام شد.","ex":"Having considered all applications, ..."},{"en":"The subject after the comma did that action.","tr":"Virgülden sonraki özne o eylemi yapan kişidir.","fa":"فاعلِ بعد از ویرگول همان کسی است که آن کار را کرده.","ex":"..., we have decided not to proceed."},{"en":"Keep the past participle: considered, spoken, reviewed.","tr":"Past participle'ı koru: considered, spoken, reviewed.","fa":"اسم مفعول را نگه دار: considered، spoken، ⁨reviewed⁩.","ex":"Having spoken to your referees, we are pleased..."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Clause","Main clause (same subject)"],"tr":["Yapı","Ana cümle (aynı özne)"],"fa":["عبارت وصفی","جمله‌ی اصلی (با همان فاعل)"]},"rows":[["Having considered all applications,","we have decided to..."],["Having reviewed your interview notes,","I would like to offer you feedback."],["Having spoken to your referees,","we are pleased to confirm your offer."]]},"body":{"en":"B2 track: open your rejection email's key sentence with a perfect participle clause, and check the subject after the comma.","tr":"B2 yolu: olumsuz yanıt e-postanın ana cümlesini bir perfect participle yapısıyla başlat ve virgülden sonraki özneyi kontrol et.","fa":"مسیر B2: جمله‌ی کلیدی ایمیل عدم پذیرش را با یک عبارت وصفی کامل شروع کن و بعد بررسی کن فاعلِ بعد از ویرگول درست باشد."}}},"grammar":{"id":"c-hr-3-4-g","level":"B1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-4","title":"Softening bad news: I'm afraid + the passive","titleTr":"Kötü haberi yumuşatmak: I'm afraid + edilgen yapı","exp":{"en":"A rejection must be clear and kind at the same time. Two tools help. First, softeners before the news: \"I'm afraid...\", \"Unfortunately...\", \"On this occasion...\". They prepare the reader without hiding the message. Second, the passive, which moves attention away from the person who decided: \"The position has been offered to another candidate.\" (not \"We gave the job to someone better\"). Form: has been / was + past participle: \"has been offered\", \"was carefully considered\". Without been, the sentence says the position did the offering: \"The position has offered...\" is wrong. Keep one clear sentence that says no; softeners must not turn it into a maybe.","tr":"Olumsuz bir yanıt aynı anda hem açık hem nazik olmalıdır. İki araç yardımcı olur. Birincisi, haberden önce yumuşatıcılar: \"I'm afraid...\", \"Unfortunately...\", \"On this occasion...\". Mesajı saklamadan okuyucuyu hazırlarlar. İkincisi, dikkati karar veren kişiden uzaklaştıran edilgen yapı: \"The position has been offered to another candidate.\" (\"We gave the job to someone better\" değil). Türkçedeki \"-ildi/-ıldı\" edilgen ekine benzer. Biçim: has been / was + past participle: \"has been offered\", \"was carefully considered\". Been olmadan cümle, teklifi pozisyonun kendisinin yaptığını söyler: \"The position has offered...\" yanlıştır. Hayır diyen tek ve açık bir cümle bırak; yumuşatıcılar onu bir \"belki\"ye çevirmemeli.","fa":"پاسخ منفی باید هم روشن باشد و هم مهربان. دو ابزار به تو کمک می‌کند. اول، عبارت‌های نرم‌کننده قبل از خبر: «⁨I'm afraid...⁩»، «⁨Unfortunately...⁩» و «⁨On this occasion...⁩». این‌ها خواننده را آماده می‌کنند، بدون اینکه پیام را پنهان کنند. دوم، فعل مجهول، که توجه را از کسی که تصمیم گرفته برمی‌دارد: «⁨The position has been offered to another candidate.⁩» (نه «We gave the job to someone better»). درست مثل «این سمت به متقاضی دیگری پیشنهاد شده است» در نامه‌های اداری فارسی. ساختار: has been یا was + اسم مفعول: «has been offered» و «was carefully considered». اگر been را جا بیندازی، معنی جمله این می‌شود که خودِ «سمت» پیشنهاد داده است؛ پس «⁨The position has offered...⁩» غلط است. در هر حال یک جمله‌ی صریح نگه دار که «نه» را بگوید؛ نرم‌کننده‌ها نباید «نه» را به «شاید» تبدیل کنند."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Move","Example"],"tr":["Hamle","Örnek"],"fa":["حرکت","مثال"]},"rows":[["Thank","Thank you for your time and interest."],["Soften","I'm afraid that on this occasion..."],["Say no (passive)","...the position has been offered to another candidate."],["Something specific and kind","We enjoyed hearing about how you trained new drivers."]]},"wrong":"Unfortunately, the position has offered to another candidate.","right":"Unfortunately, the position has been offered to another candidate.","blank":{"sentence":"Unfortunately, the position ___ to another candidate.","word":"has been offered","distractors":["has offered","is offering"]},"wrong2":"A decision has been make.","right2":"A decision has been made.","blank2":{"sentence":"Your application ___ carefully considered.","word":"was","distractors":["did","has"]},"expParts":{"tryFrom":"blank","hook":{"en":"Leyla's first draft was true but felt like a door closing on Karim's fingers. Two tools made it kind.","tr":"Leyla'nın ilk taslağı doğruydu ama Karim'in parmaklarına kapanan bir kapı gibiydi. İki araç onu nazik hâle getirdi.","fa":"پیش‌نویس اول لیلا درست بود، ولی مثل دری بود که روی انگشت‌های کریم بسته شود. دو ابزار زبانی مهربانش کرد."},"tryWhy":{"en":"has been offered: the position does not offer anything; it is offered. The passive needs been.","tr":"has been offered: pozisyon bir şey teklif etmez; o teklif edilir. Edilgen yapı been ister.","fa":"جواب has been offered است: موقعیت شغلی چیزی پیشنهاد نمی‌دهد؛ به کسی پیشنهاد داده می‌شود. مجهول به been نیاز دارد."},"rule":[{"en":"Prepare the reader: I'm afraid, unfortunately, on this occasion.","tr":"Okuru hazırla: I'm afraid, unfortunately, on this occasion.","fa":"خواننده را آماده کن: I'm afraid، unfortunately، ⁨on this occasion⁩.","ex":"I'm afraid that on this occasion..."},{"en":"Passive: has been / was + past participle.","tr":"Edilgen: has been / was + past participle.","fa":"مجهول با has been یا was و اسم مفعول ساخته می‌شود.","ex":"The position has been offered to another candidate."},{"en":"Keep one clear sentence that says no.","tr":"'Hayır' diyen net bir cümle mutlaka olsun.","fa":"حتماً یک جمله‌ی روشن بگذار که «نه» را بگوید.","ex":"...the position has been offered to another candidate."}],"test":{"en":"Ask: who did the action? If the subject did not do it (the position, a decision), you need been.","tr":"Sor: eylemi kim yaptı? Özne yapmadıysa (the position, a decision) been gerekir.","fa":"بپرس: چه کسی کار را انجام داد؟ اگر فاعل جمله انجامش نداده (the position، a decision)، been لازم است."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish uses -ildi ('pozisyon başka bir adaya verildi') and Persian shode ast, so the passive idea is familiar. The trap is dropping been: English needs has been + past participle.","tr":"Türkçede edilgen '-ildi' ile yapılır: 'Pozisyon başka bir adaya verildi.' Anlam tanıdıktır; tuzak been'i unutmaktır: has been offered.","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «این موقعیت به متقاضی دیگری داده شد» و ساختار مجهول آشناست. تله این است که been را جا بیندازی: «has been offered»."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["position has offered","position was offer","has been make","has been give","decision has made","application has considered"],"fix":{"en":"In the passive keep been + past participle: 'The position has been offered...', 'A decision has been made.'","tr":"Edilgende been + past participle kullan: 'The position has been offered...', 'A decision has been made.'","fa":"در مجهول been و اسم مفعول بیاور: «The position has been offered...» و «A decision has been made.»"}},{"find":["you were not successful because","someone better","less experience than the other candidates"],"fix":{"en":"True, but it can sound like blame. Try the passive with one honest reason and one thing they did well.","tr":"Doğru ama suçlama gibi duyulabilir. Edilgen yapı, dürüst bir neden ve iyi yaptığı bir şeyle dene.","fa":"درست است، ولی ممکن است سرزنش‌آمیز به نظر برسد. با مجهول، یک دلیل صادقانه و یک کار خوبِ او دوباره بنویس."}}]},"b2":{"id":"c-hr-3-4-b2","level":"B2","track":"B2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-4","title":"Having considered...: perfect participle clauses","titleTr":"Having considered...: perfect participle yapıları","exp":{"en":"Formal HR letters often open with a perfect participle clause (having + past participle) to show that one action was finished before the next: \"Having considered all applications carefully, we have decided to offer the role to another candidate.\" The rule that catches many writers: the person who did the considering must be the subject of the main clause. \"Having considered your application, it was decided not to proceed\" is wrong, because \"it\" did not consider anything (a dangling participle). Write \"we have decided\" after the comma. Also keep the past participle: \"Having considered\", never \"Having consider\".","tr":"Resmî İK yazıları, bir eylemin diğerinden önce bittiğini göstermek için çoğu zaman perfect participle yapısıyla (having + past participle) başlar: \"Having considered all applications carefully, we have decided to offer the role to another candidate.\" Türkçedeki \"değerlendirdikten sonra\" yapısına benzer. Birçok yazarı yakalayan kural: değerlendirmeyi yapan kişi ana cümlenin öznesi olmalıdır. \"Having considered your application, it was decided not to proceed\" yanlıştır, çünkü \"it\" hiçbir şeyi değerlendirmedi (buna dangling participle denir). Virgülden sonra \"we have decided\" yaz. Past participle'ı da koru: \"Having considered\", asla \"Having consider\" değil.","fa":"نامه‌های رسمی منابع انسانی اغلب با یک عبارت وصفی کامل (having + اسم مفعول) شروع می‌شوند تا نشان دهند کاری پیش از کار بعدی تمام شده است: «⁨Having considered all applications carefully, we have decided to offer the role to another candidate.⁩» معادلش در نامه‌های اداری فارسی می‌شود «پس از بررسی دقیق همه‌ی درخواست‌ها...». قاعده‌ای که خیلی‌ها را به اشتباه می‌اندازد: کسی که «بررسی کرده» باید فاعل جمله‌ی اصلی باشد. جمله‌ی «Having considered your application, it was decided not to proceed» غلط است، چون it چیزی را بررسی نکرده است (به این خطا dangling participle می‌گویند). بعد از ویرگول بنویس «we have decided». اسم مفعول را هم فراموش نکن: «Having considered»، نه «Having consider»."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Clause","Main clause (same subject)"],"tr":["Yapı","Ana cümle (aynı özne)"],"fa":["عبارت وصفی","جمله‌ی اصلی (با همان فاعل)"]},"rows":[["Having considered all applications,","we have decided to..."],["Having reviewed your interview notes,","I would like to offer you feedback."],["Having spoken to your referees,","we are pleased to confirm your offer."]]},"wrong":"Having considered your application, it was decided not to proceed.","right":"Having considered your application, we have decided not to proceed.","blank":{"sentence":"___ all applications carefully, we have decided to offer the role to another candidate.","word":"Having considered","distractors":["Considered","Having consider"]},"wrong2":"Having consider all applications, we have decided not to proceed.","right2":"Having considered all applications, we have decided not to proceed.","blank2":{"sentence":"Having spoken to your referees, ___ pleased to confirm your offer.","word":"we are","distractors":["it is","the offer is"]},"useIn":{"en":"B2 track: open your rejection email's key sentence with a perfect participle clause, and check the subject after the comma.","tr":"B2 yolu: olumsuz yanıt e-postanın ana cümlesini bir perfect participle yapısıyla başlat ve virgülden sonraki özneyi kontrol et.","fa":"مسیر B2: جمله‌ی کلیدی ایمیل عدم پذیرش را با یک عبارت وصفی کامل شروع کن و بعد بررسی کن فاعلِ بعد از ویرگول درست باشد."},"exitItem":{"from":"hr-3-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"___ your interview notes, we would like to invite you to a second meeting.","options":["Having reviewed","Reviewed","Having review"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Having reviewed: 'having' + past participle shows one action finished before the next. 'Reviewed' alone changes the meaning, and 'having review' drops -ed.","tr":"Having reviewed: 'having' + üçüncü hâl, bir eylemin bir sonrakinden önce bittiğini gösterir. Tek başına 'Reviewed' anlamı değiştirir; 'having review' -ed'i düşürür.","fa":"⁨Having reviewed⁩ درست است، چون ⁨having⁩ و اسم مفعول نشان می‌دهد کاری قبل از کار بعدی تمام شده. ⁨reviewed⁩ تنها معنی را عوض می‌کند و ⁨having review⁩ ⁨-ed⁩ ندارد."}},"expParts":{"hook":{"en":"'Having considered all applications, we have decided...' One clause shows the careful work came first.","tr":"'Having considered all applications, we have decided...' Tek bir yapı önce özenli bir değerlendirme yapıldığını gösterir.","fa":"«⁨Having considered all applications, we have decided...⁩» همین یک عبارت نشان می‌دهد که اول همه چیز با دقت بررسی شده است."},"tryWhy":{"en":"we are: the people who spoke to the referees must be the subject after the comma.","tr":"we are: referanslarla konuşanlar virgülden sonra özne olmalı.","fa":"جواب we are است: کسانی که با معرف‌ها حرف زده‌اند باید بعد از ویرگول فاعل جمله باشند."},"rule":[{"en":"Having + past participle = this was done first.","tr":"Having + past participle = bu önce yapıldı.","fa":"ساختار Having و اسم مفعول یعنی این کار اول انجام شد.","ex":"Having considered all applications, ..."},{"en":"The subject after the comma did that action.","tr":"Virgülden sonraki özne o eylemi yapan kişidir.","fa":"فاعلِ بعد از ویرگول همان کسی است که آن کار را کرده.","ex":"..., we have decided not to proceed."},{"en":"Keep the past participle: considered, spoken, reviewed.","tr":"Past participle'ı koru: considered, spoken, reviewed.","fa":"اسم مفعول را نگه دار: considered، spoken، ⁨reviewed⁩.","ex":"Having spoken to your referees, we are pleased..."}],"test":{"en":"Ask the main clause: did you do the considering? If the answer is 'it' or 'the offer', rewrite with we.","tr":"Ana cümleye sor: değerlendirmeyi sen mi yaptın? Cevap 'it' ya da 'the offer' ise we ile yeniden yaz.","fa":"از جمله‌ی اصلی بپرس: تو بررسی کردی؟ اگر جواب «it» یا «the offer» است، با we دوباره بنویس."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish -dikten sonra and Persian pas az barresi let the subject stay hidden. In English the subject after the comma must be the person who did the first action.","tr":"Türkçede 'Tüm başvuruları değerlendirdikten sonra...' derken özne gizli kalabilir. İngilizcede virgülden sonraki özne, ilk eylemi yapan kişi olmak zorundadır: we.","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «پس از بررسی همه‌ی درخواست‌ها تصمیم گرفته شد...» و فاعل پنهان می‌ماند. در انگلیسی فاعلِ بعد از ویرگول باید همان کسی باشد که کار اول را کرده: ⁨we⁩."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["having consider","having review","application, it was decided","applications, it was decided","referees, it is"],"fix":{"en":"Use having + past participle, and make we the subject: 'Having considered your application, we have decided...'","tr":"having + past participle kullan ve we'yi özne yap: 'Having considered your application, we have decided...'","fa":"having و اسم مفعول بیاور و we را فاعل کن: «Having considered your application, we have decided...»"}}]},"vocab":{"id":"c-hr-3-4-v","level":"B1","category":"vocab","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-4","goals":["career"],"title":{"en":"Offers and Rejections","tr":"Teklifler ve Olumsuz Yanıtlar","fa":"پیشنهاد کار و پاسخ منفی"},"cards":[{"word":"job offer","sentence":"I'm calling to make you a job offer.","meaning":{"en":"A formal invitation to take a job.","tr":"iş teklifi.","fa":"پیشنهاد شغلی (دعوت رسمی به پذیرفتن یک شغل)"}},{"word":"accept","sentence":"Deniz accepted the offer on the phone.","gap":"accepted","accept":["accepted","accept"],"meaning":{"en":"To say yes to something offered.","tr":"kabul etmek.","fa":"پذیرفتن"}},{"word":"decline","sentence":"She declined the offer because of the location.","gap":"declined","accept":["declined","decline"],"meaning":{"en":"To say no politely.","tr":"kibarca reddetmek.","fa":"مؤدبانه رد کردن"}},{"word":"subject to","sentence":"The offer is subject to two references.","meaning":{"en":"Depending on something happening first.","tr":"... şartına bağlı.","fa":"مشروط به؛ منوط به"}},{"word":"start date","sentence":"Your start date is the first of April.","meaning":{"en":"The first day of the new job.","tr":"işe başlama tarihi.","fa":"تاریخ شروع به کار"}},{"word":"unsuccessful","sentence":"We write to every unsuccessful candidate.","meaning":{"en":"Not chosen; did not get the result wanted.","tr":"seçilmeyen; başvurusu olumsuz sonuçlanan.","fa":"ناموفق؛ انتخاب‌نشده"}},{"word":"on this occasion","sentence":"On this occasion, we will not be moving forward.","meaning":{"en":"This time (softens a no).","tr":"bu sefer.","fa":"این بار؛ در این مرحله (برای نرم کردن «نه»)"}},{"word":"keep your details on file","sentence":"With your permission, we will keep your details on file.","meaning":{"en":"To save your information for future jobs.","tr":"bilgilerini ileride kullanmak üzere saklamak.","fa":"اطلاعاتت را برای فرصت‌های بعدی نگه داشتن (در بانک اطلاعات متقاضیان)"}},{"word":"feedback","sentence":"Would you like some feedback on your interview?","meaning":{"en":"Comments on how well someone did.","tr":"geri bildirim.","fa":"بازخورد"}},{"word":"in writing","sentence":"I'll send the offer in writing today.","meaning":{"en":"On paper or by email, not only spoken.","tr":"yazılı olarak.","fa":"کتبی (روی کاغذ یا با ایمیل، نه فقط شفاهی)"}}]},"story":{"id":"c-hr-3-4-s","level":"B1","genre":"Workplace","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-4","title":{"en":"Two Phone Calls","tr":"İki Telefon","fa":"دو تماس تلفنی"},"text":"On Friday morning Leyla had one call to make and one email to write. She made the easy call first.\n\n\"Deniz, it's Leyla from Atlas. I'm calling with good news. We'd like to offer you the driver position in Dubai.\"\n\nSilence. Then a laugh, the kind people make when they are trying not to shout. \"Really? Sorry. Yes. Yes, I accept.\"\n\n\"Wonderful. The offer is subject to two references, and the start date is the first of April. I'll send everything in writing today. Do you have any questions?\"\n\n\"Can you say the date again? I want to write it on the wall.\"\n\nThe email was harder. Karim had been good, just not the best fit for the night routes. Her first draft said: \"You were not successful because you have less experience than the other candidates.\"\n\nShe read it and winced. It was true, but it sounded like a door closing on his fingers.\n\nSelin looked over her shoulder. \"Will he learn anything from that line? Or will he just feel small?\"\n\nLeyla deleted it and started again. Thank him first. Then one clear sentence: I'm afraid that on this occasion the position has been offered to another candidate. Then one true, specific thing he had done well.\n\nShe did not know that the night before, across the city, Karim had opened the small notebook he kept for every job application and written:\n\n\"Atlas, day 9 of waiting. I think the interview went well. The HR woman smiled when I talked about training the new drivers. If it's a no, I just want to know why. I can take a no. I can't take silence.\"","vocab":[{"word":"wince","en":"To make a small face because something hurts or feels wrong.","tr":"yüzünü buruşturmak","fa":"از درد یا ناخوشایندی چهره در هم کشیدن"},{"word":"fit","en":"Here: how well a person matches a job.","tr":"uyum","fa":"تناسب (میزان جور بودن فرد با شغل)"},{"word":"draft","en":"A first version of a text.","tr":"taslak","fa":"پیش‌نویس"},{"word":"notebook","en":"A small book for writing notes.","tr":"defter","fa":"دفترچه"},{"word":"silence","en":"Here: getting no answer at all.","tr":"sessizlik, cevapsız kalmak","fa":"سکوت؛ بی‌جوابی (هیچ پاسخی نگرفتن)"}],"quiz":[{"prompt":"What does \"The offer is subject to two references\" mean?","options":["Deniz must write two references","The offer depends on two good references","Two people will call Deniz"],"correct":1},{"prompt":"Choose the correct sentence.","options":["The position has been offered to another candidate.","The position has offered to another candidate.","The position is offering to another candidate."],"correct":0},{"prompt":"Why did Leyla delete her first draft?","options":["It had a grammar mistake","It was true but cold, and Karim could not learn from it","Selin wrote a better one"],"correct":1},{"prompt":"What does Karim fear most?","options":["A no","A long email","Hearing nothing at all"],"correct":2}],"notice":{"en":"Leyla makes an easy call and writes a hard email. Look at her first draft: what is wrong with a sentence that is true?","tr":"Leyla kolay bir telefon görüşmesi yapıyor ve zor bir e-posta yazıyor. İlk taslağa bak: doğru bir cümlede ne yanlış olabilir?","fa":"لیلا یک تماس آسان می‌گیرد و یک ایمیل سخت می‌نویسد. به پیش‌نویس اول نگاه کن: جمله‌ای که درست است چه ایرادی می‌تواند داشته باشد؟"},"bridge":{"en":"'I'm afraid that on this occasion the position has been offered...' Next: see how softeners and the passive work.","tr":"'I'm afraid that on this occasion the position has been offered...' Sırada: yumuşatma ifadeleri ve edilgen yapının nasıl çalıştığını gör.","fa":"«⁨I'm afraid that on this occasion the position has been offered...⁩» قدم بعد: ببین عبارت‌های نرم‌کننده و مجهول چطور کار می‌کنند."}},"speaking":{"id":"hr-3-4","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-4","topic":{"en":"Making a Job Offer by Phone","tr":"Telefonla İş Teklifi Yapmak","fa":"پیشنهاد کار پشت تلفن"},"warmup":{"en":"Think of the best and the worst news you ever got by phone. What did the caller do well or badly?","tr":"Telefonla aldığın en iyi ve en kötü haberi düşün. Arayan kişi neyi iyi ya da kötü yaptı?","fa":"بهترین و بدترین خبری را که تا حالا تلفنی شنیده‌ای به یاد بیاور. تماس‌گیرنده چه کاری را خوب یا بد انجام داد؟"},"questions":[{"en":"Open the call, check it is a good time, and give the good news.","tr":"Görüşmeyi aç, uygun bir zaman olup olmadığını sor ve iyi haberi ver.","fa":"تماس را شروع کن، بپرس وقت مناسبی برای صحبت است یا نه، و خبر خوب را بده."},{"en":"Give two conditions: the start date and \"subject to references\".","tr":"İki koşul söyle: başlama tarihi ve \"subject to references\".","fa":"دو شرط را بگو: تاریخ شروع به کار و اینکه پیشنهاد منوط به استعلام از معرف‌هاست («subject to references»)."},{"en":"The candidate asks: \"Is the salary negotiable?\" Answer politely and promise a reply time.","tr":"Aday soruyor: \"Maaş pazarlığa açık mı?\" Kibarca cevap ver ve bir dönüş zamanı söz ver.","fa":"متقاضی می‌پرسد: «⁨Is the salary negotiable?⁩» مؤدبانه جواب بده و بگو تا کی خبرش را می‌دهی."}],"followups":[{"en":"Say the whole offer call in 90 seconds, then 60, then 45.","tr":"Teklif görüşmesinin tamamını 90, sonra 60, sonra 45 saniyede söyle.","fa":"کل تماس پیشنهاد کار را یک بار در ۹۰ ثانیه، بعد در ۶۰ و بعد در ۴۵ ثانیه بگو."},{"en":"Now call Karim before the email arrives: tell him the outcome kindly in 30 seconds.","tr":"Şimdi e-posta gelmeden önce Karim'i ara: sonucu 30 saniyede nazikçe söyle.","fa":"حالا پیش از اینکه ایمیل به دست کریم برسد، به او زنگ بزن و در ۳۰ ثانیه، با مهربانی، نتیجه را بگو."},{"en":"Then call Deniz's last employer for a reference: confirm his job title, his dates and whether they would employ him again. Ask for facts, not opinions.","tr":"Sonra referans için Deniz'in son işverenini ara: iş unvanını, çalışma tarihlerini ve onu yeniden işe alıp almayacaklarını teyit et. Görüş değil, bilgi iste.","fa":"بعد برای استعلام به کارفرمای قبلی دنیز زنگ بزن: عنوان شغلی و تاریخ‌های کارش را تأیید کن و بپرس آیا حاضرند دوباره استخدامش کنند. واقعیت بخواه، نه نظر شخصی."},{"en":"Now give one piece of bad news you may really have to give, kindly and clearly.","tr":"Şimdi gerçekten vermek zorunda kalabileceğin bir kötü haberi nazikçe ve net biçimde ver.","fa":"حالا خبر بدی را که شاید واقعاً مجبور شوی بدهی، محترمانه و روشن بگو."}],"expressions":[{"phrase":"I'm calling with good news.","meaning":{"en":"Opens an offer call.","tr":"Teklif görüşmesini açar.","fa":"تماسِ پیشنهاد کار را شروع می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"The offer is subject to...","meaning":{"en":"States a condition.","tr":"Bir koşul belirtir.","fa":"یک شرط را می‌گوید."}},{"phrase":"I'm afraid that on this occasion...","meaning":{"en":"Softens a no without hiding it.","tr":"Hayırı saklamadan yumuşatır.","fa":"«نه» را نرم می‌کند، بدون اینکه پنهانش کند."}}],"culture":{"en":"In many UK and US companies, candidates rejected at the final stage often get a short call or an offer of feedback, while earlier-stage candidates get an email. In many markets candidates simply hear nothing, which hurts the employer's reputation. A short, kind, specific message takes five minutes.","tr":"Birçok İngiliz ve Amerikan şirketinde son aşamada elenen adaylar çoğu zaman kısa bir telefon ya da geri bildirim teklifi alır; daha erken aşamadakiler e-posta alır. Birçok pazarda adaylara hiç dönüş yapılmaz ve bu işverenin itibarına zarar verir. Kısa, nazik ve somut bir mesaj beş dakika sürer.","fa":"در بسیاری از شرکت‌های بریتانیا و آمریکا، متقاضیانی که در مرحله‌ی آخر انتخاب نمی‌شوند معمولاً یک تماس کوتاه یا پیشنهاد بازخورد می‌گیرند و متقاضیان مراحل اول یک ایمیل. در خیلی از بازارهای کار هم اصلاً هیچ جوابی به متقاضی داده نمی‌شود؛ تجربه‌ای که شاید برای تو هم آشنا باشد و به اعتبار کارفرما ضربه می‌زند. یک پیام کوتاه، مهربان و مشخص فقط پنج دقیقه وقت می‌گیرد."},"model":"Hi Deniz, it's Leyla from Atlas. Is this a good time to talk? Great. I'm calling with good news. We'd like to offer you the driver position in Dubai. The start date is the first of April, and the offer is subject to two references and your work permit. I'll send everything in writing today. About the salary, I'll check with finance and call you back by Monday.","selfCheck":[{"en":"I checked it was a good time before the news.","tr":"Haberi vermeden önce uygun bir zaman olup olmadığını sordum.","fa":"پیش از دادن خبر پرسیدم آیا زمان مناسبی است."},{"en":"I gave the start date and 'subject to references'.","tr":"Başlangıç tarihini ve 'subject to references' şartını söyledim.","fa":"تاریخ شروع و شرط «subject to references» را گفتم."},{"en":"I promised a clear reply time for the salary question.","tr":"Maaş sorusu için net bir cevap zamanı verdim.","fa":"برای سؤال حقوق، زمان مشخصی برای جواب دادن قول دادم."},{"en":"In the 30-second call to Karim, the no was clear and kind.","tr":"Karim'le 30 saniyelik görüşmede 'hayır' net ve nazikti.","fa":"در تماس ۳۰ ثانیه‌ای با کریم، «نه» روشن و مهربان بود."}]},"writing":{"id":"c-hr-3-4-w","title":{"en":"The rejection email to Karim","tr":"Karim'e olumsuz yanıt e-postası","fa":"ایمیل عدم پذیرش برای کریم"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-4","type":"writing","difficulty":"medium","prompt":{"en":"Write the rejection email to Karim (60-90 words): thank him, one clear softened no with the passive, one honest reason, one specific thing he did well, and a kind close.","tr":"Karim'e olumsuz yanıt e-postasını yaz (60-90 kelime): teşekkür et, edilgen yapıyla yumuşatılmış açık bir hayır, dürüst bir sebep, iyi yaptığı somut bir şey ve nazik bir kapanış.","fa":"ایمیل عدم پذیرش را برای کریم بنویس (۶۰ تا ۹۰ کلمه): از او تشکر کن، یک «نه»ی روشن و نرم با فعل مجهول بگو، یک دلیل صادقانه بیاور، به یک کار مشخص که خوب انجام داد اشاره کن و با لحنی مهربان تمام کن."},"model":"Dear Karim, Thank you for your time and for coming to the interview last week. We enjoyed hearing how you trained two new drivers in your last job. I'm afraid that on this occasion the position has been offered to another candidate with more night-route experience. This was a difficult decision. With your permission, we would like to keep your details on file for future day-route roles. I wish you every success. Kind regards, Leyla Karimi","frame":"Dear ___, Thank you for ___. We enjoyed hearing ___. I'm afraid that on this occasion the position has been offered to ___. This was ___. With your permission, we would like to ___. I wish you ___. Kind regards, ___","words":[{"word":"afraid"},{"word":"occasion"},{"word":"offered"}],"minWords":60,"minSentences":6,"rubric":["Task done: thanks, clear no, reason, specific praise, close","Organised: positive start, the news, the reason, the future, close","Language: passive (has been offered); I'm afraid / on this occasion","Tone: kind and clear; no false hope, no blame"],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: teşekkür, net bir hayır, sebep, somut övgü, kapanış","Düzen: olumlu giriş, haber, sebep, gelecek, kapanış","Dil: edilgen (has been offered); I'm afraid / on this occasion","Üslup: nazik ve net; boş umut yok, suçlama yok"],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: تشکر، «نه»ی روشن، دلیل، تعریف مشخص، پایان","نظم: شروع مثبت، خبر، دلیل، آینده، پایان","زبان: مجهول (has been offered)؛ I'm afraid / on this occasion","لحن: مهربان و روشن؛ بدون امید واهی و بدون سرزنش"]},"portfolio":"hr-final-5","parts":[{"t":{"en":"Thanks","tr":"Teşekkür","fa":"تشکر"},"find":["thank you"],"sample":"thanks for coming to the interview last week"},{"t":{"en":"One specific strength","tr":"Somut bir güçlü yön","fa":"یک نقطه‌ی قوت مشخص"},"find":["we enjoyed","we were impressed"],"sample":"how he trained two new drivers"},{"t":{"en":"The clear no","tr":"Net ret","fa":"«نه» روشن"},"find":["i'm afraid","on this occasion","has been offered"],"sample":"the position has been offered to another candidate"},{"t":{"en":"An honest reason","tr":"Dürüst bir gerekçe","fa":"یک دلیل صادقانه"},"find":["with more","because","experience"],"sample":"another candidate had more night-route experience"},{"t":{"en":"A kind close","tr":"Kibar bir kapanış","fa":"پایانی مهربان"},"find":["wish you","keep your details","success"],"sample":"details kept on file; every success"}]},"perspective":{"id":"c-hr-3-4-p","title":{"en":"Karim the night before","tr":"Önceki gece Karim","fa":"کریم، شب قبل"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-4","type":"perspective","minSentences":2,"prompt":{"en":"Read Karim's notebook entry again. You are Karim the night before the email. Write 2-3 sentences in first person: what do you hope it says, and what do you need to read even if the answer is no?","tr":"Karim'in defterine yazdıklarını yeniden oku. E-postadan önceki gece Karim'sin. Birinci tekil şahısla 2-3 cümle yaz: e-postada ne yazmasını umuyorsun ve cevap hayır olsa bile ne okumaya ihtiyacın var?","fa":"یادداشت کریم در دفترچه‌اش را دوباره بخوان. تو کریم هستی، شب قبل از رسیدن ایمیل. از زبان خودت دو یا سه جمله بنویس: امیدواری در ایمیل چه نوشته شده باشد، و حتی اگر جواب منفی باشد، دوست داری چه چیزی در آن بخوانی؟"}},"exit":{"id":"c-hr-3-4-x","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-4","type":"exit","items":[{"from":"hr-3-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"I'm afraid the role ___ to an internal candidate.","options":["has been given","has given","is giving"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"has been given: the role receives the action, so has been + past participle. 'Has given' says the role gave something, and 'is giving' is wrong for news.","tr":"has been given: görev eylemi alır, bu yüzden has been + üçüncü hâl. 'Has given' görevin bir şey verdiğini söyler; 'is giving' bir haber için yanlıştır.","fa":"has been given درست است، چون سمت به کسی داده شده و has been و اسم مفعول لازم است. has given یعنی خود سمت چیزی داده و is giving برای خبر غلط است."}},{"from":"hr-3-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"All applications ___ read by two people.","options":["were","did","had"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"were: the applications received the action, so were + past participle (read). 'Did' and 'had' don't make the passive.","tr":"were: başvurular eylemi aldı, bu yüzden were + üçüncü hâl (read). 'Did' ve 'had' edilgen yapı kurmaz.","fa":"were درست است، چون درخواست‌ها خوانده شدند و were و اسم مفعول لازم است. did و had مجهول نمی‌سازند."}},{"from":"hr-3-4","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which rejection line is kind and clear?","options":["You failed the interview.","Maybe next time, who knows?","I'm afraid that on this occasion we will not be moving forward."],"correct":2,"point":1,"why":{"en":"'I'm afraid that on this occasion we will not be moving forward' is clear and kind. 'You failed' is harsh, and 'Maybe next time, who knows?' is vague.","tr":"'I'm afraid that on this occasion we will not be moving forward' net ve naziktir. 'You failed' serttir; 'Maybe next time, who knows?' belirsizdir.","fa":"«I'm afraid that on this occasion we will not be moving forward» روشن و مهربان است. You failed تند است و «Maybe next time, who knows?» مبهم است."}},{"from":"hr-3-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"He ___ us he could start immediately.","options":["said","told","explained"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"told: 'tell' takes a person (told us). 'Said' takes no person after it, and 'explained' would need 'to us'.","tr":"told: 'tell' bir kişi alır (told us). 'Said' kendinden sonra kişi almaz; 'explained' 'to us' ister.","fa":"told درست است، چون tell شخص می‌خواهد (told us). بعد از said شخص نمی‌آید و explained به to us نیاز دارد."}},{"from":"hr-3-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"Then I ___ going to ask you about your past jobs.","options":["am","will","have"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"am: 'going to' needs be before it: I am going to ask. 'Will' and 'have' don't go with going to.","tr":"am: 'going to' öncesinde be ister: I am going to ask. 'Will' ve 'have' going to ile gelmez.","fa":"am درست است، چون قبل از going to فعل be لازم است: I am going to ask. will و have با going to نمی‌آیند."}},{"from":"hr-2-1","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which is a DESIRABLE requirement?","options":["Candidates must hold a Class C licence.","Knowledge of Arabic would be an advantage.","You will plan daily routes."],"correct":1,"point":1,"why":{"en":"'Knowledge of Arabic would be an advantage' is desirable: nice to have. 'Must hold' is essential, and 'you will plan routes' is a duty.","tr":"'Knowledge of Arabic would be an advantage' istenen bir artıdır. 'Must hold' zorunludur; 'you will plan routes' bir görevdir.","fa":"«Knowledge of Arabic would be an advantage» یعنی بودنش خوب است. must hold ضروری است و you will plan routes یک وظیفه است."}}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
